      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the simplified value of the fourth term of the sequence, we need to determine the sum of the first four consecutive powers of 3:\n\n- The first term is \\(3^0 = 1\\).\n- The second term is \\(3^0 + 3^1 = 1 + 3 = 4\\).\n- The third term is \\(3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 = 1 + 3 + 9 = 13\\).\n- The fourth term is \\(3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3 = 1 + 3 + 9 + 27 = 40\\).\n\nWe can also express the general term of this sequence as the sum of a geometric series. The sequence is \\(1, 4, 13, 40, \\ldots\\). This can be written as:\n\n\\[\na_1 = 3^0 + 3^0 = 1 + 1 = 2\n\\]\n\\[\na_2 = 3^0 + 3^1 = 1 + 3 = 4\n\\]\n\\[\na_3 = 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 = 1 + 3 + 9 = 13\n\\]\n\\[\na_4 = 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + 3^3 = 1 + 3 + 9 + 27 = 40\n\\]\n\nThe general term of the sequence can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\na_n = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} 3^k = \\frac{3^n - 1}{3 - 1} = \\frac{3^n - 1}{2}\n\\]\n\nFor the fourth term (\\(n = 4\\)):\n\n\\[\na_4 = \\frac{3^4 - 1}{2} = \\frac{81 - 1}{2} = \\frac{80}{2} = 40\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified value of the fourth term of the sequence is \\(\\boxed{40}\\).",
